ner; Designing user interfaces, improving user experience, conducting user research; Project: All projects (focusing on user experience)  |  sophiarodriguez@example.com  |  October 9, 2024   \\nWang Fang  wang_fang  AI Researcher (AI Team); Designing and implementing machine learning models, optimizing model performance; Project: OpenHands (LLM project); Skills: Python, machine learning, LLM  |  wangfang@example.com  |  October 9, 2024   \\nZhang Wei  zhang_wei  Senior Software Engineer (Streaming Database Team); Developing and optimizing core streaming database functionalities; Project: RisingWave (Streaming Database); Skills: Rust, database systems  |  zhangwei@example.com  |  October 9, 2024   \\ntheagentcompany  theagentcompany  |  theagentcompany@example.com  |  October 19, 2024   \\n  \\n<::before>\\n\\nShowing results 1 - 18 of 18 \\n\\n  1. _\\ue010_\\n  2. 1 \\n  3. _\\ue010_\\n\\n\\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:3000/directory/users', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', screenshot_path='/outputs/.browser_screenshots/screenshot_20251103_031452_688534.png', error=False, observation=<ObservationType.BROWSE: 'browse'>, goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:3000/directory/users'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"\\n\\nclick('572')  # Users tab\\nnoop(2000)  # Wait for users to load\\n\\n\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='857'), CmdRunAction(command='\\npython3 -c \"import pptx\" 2>&1 || pip3 install python-pptx\\n', is_input=False, thought=\"Perfect! I can see all the leadership team members in the Users directory. Let me collect the information for the required positions:\\n\\n1. CTO: Sarah Johnson\\n2. Sales Director: Mark Johnson  \\n3. Marketing Manager: Jessica Lee\\n4. Finance Director: David Wong\\n5. Human Resources Manager: Chen Xinyi\\n\\nNow I'll create the PowerPoint presentation. First, let me check if python-pptx is installed, and if not, install it.\", blocking=False, is_static=False, cwd=None, hidden=False, action=<ActionType.RUN: 'run'>, confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None), CmdOutputObservation(content='', command='python3 -c \"import pptx\" 2>&1 || pip3 install python-pptx', observation=<ObservationType.RUN: 'run'>, metadata=CmdOutputMetadata(exit_code=0, pid=-1, username='root', hostname='ecs-d984', working_dir='/outputs', py_interpreter_path='/openhands/poetry/openhands-ai-5O4_aCHf-py3.12/bin/python', prefix='', suffix='\\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]'), hidden=False), **FileEditAction**\nPath: [/workspace/create_presentation.py]\nThought: Great! The python-pptx library is already installed. Now I'll create the Python script to generate the PowerPoint presentation with the leadership information I collected from RocketChat.\nCommand: create\nCreated File with Text:\n```\n\nfrom pptx import Presentation\nfrom pptx.util import Inches, Pt\nfrom pptx.enum.text import PP_ALIGN\nfrom pptx.dml.color import RGBColor\n\ndef create_leadership_presentation():\n    # Leadership data collected from RocketChat directory\n    leadership_data = [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Sarah Johnson\",\n            \"position\": \"CTO\",\n            \"intro\": \"Technical strategy planning, R&D team leadership, new technology assessment; Oversees all technical projects\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Mark Johnson\", \n            \"position\": \"Sales Director\",\n            \"intro\": \"Developing sales strategies, managing sales team, expanding client relationships; Project: N/A (Sales)\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Jessica Lee\",\n            \"position\": \"Marketing Manager\", \n            \"intro\": \"Developing marketing strategies, managing brand image, organizing marketing events; Project: N/A (Marketing)\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"David Wong\",\n            \"position\": \"Finance Director\",\n            \"intro\": \"Financial planning, budget management, financial reporting; Project: N/A (Finance)\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Chen Xinyi\",\n            \"position\": \"Human Resources Manager\",\n            \"intro\": \"Recruitment, employee training, compensation management; Project: N/A (HR)\"\n        }\n    ]\n    \n    # Create a new presentation\n    prs = Presentation()\n    \n    # Title slide\n    title_slide_layout = prs.slide_layouts[0]\n    slide = prs.slides.add_slide(title_slide_layout)\n    title = slide.shapes.title\n    subtitle = slide.placeholders[1]\n    \n    title.text = \"Leadership Team\"\n    subtitle.text = \"Company Leadership Introduction\"\n    \n    # Create slides for each leadership position\n    for leader in leadership_data:\n        # Use a content layout for leadership slides\n        content_slide_layout = prs.slide_layouts[1]\n        slide = prs.slides.add_slide(content_slide_layout)\n        \n        # Title (position)\n        title_shape = slide.shapes.title\n        title_shape.text = leader[\"position\"]\n        \n        # Content (name and introduction)\n        content_shape = slide.placeholders[1]\n        text_frame = content_shape.text_frame\n        text_frame.clear()  # Clear default text\n        \n        # Add name\n        p = text_frame.paragraphs[0]\n        p.text = leader[\"name\"]\n        p.font.size = Pt(24)\n        p.font.bold = True\n        p.font.color.rgb = RGBColor(0, 0, 0)\n        \n        # Add introduction\n        p = text_frame.add_paragraph()\n        p.text = leader[\"intro\"]\n        p.font.size = Pt(18)\n        p.font.color.rgb = RGBColor(64, 64, 64)\n        p.space_after = Pt(12)\n    \n    # Save the presentation\n    prs.save('/workspace/leadership_intro.pptx')\n    print(\"Presentation created successfully at /workspace/leadership_intro.pptx\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    create_leadership_presentation()\n\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /workspace/create_pr